{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-4a6d5c0b-1d08-491b-a8b0-a0959de37b26-23\nfc_4280e92c-49a8-98c7-825d-5337817199c5_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"which loom; cd /work/ws && loom --help 2>&1 | head -40; cd /work/ws && loom data --help 2>&1 | head -40","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-4a6d5c0b-1d08-491b-a8b0-a0959de37b26-23\nfc_4280e92c-49a8-98c7-825d-5337817199c5_0","simpleCommands":["which","cd","loom","head","cd","loom","head"],"hasInputRedirect":false,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"which","args":[{"type":"word","value":"loom"}],"fullText":"which loom"},{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws"}],"fullText":"cd /work/ws"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"--help"}],"fullText":"loom --help"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-40"}],"fullText":"head -40"},{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws"}],"fullText":"cd /work/ws"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"--help"}],"fullText":"loom data --help"},{"name":"head","args":[{"type":"number","value":"-40"}],"fullText":"head -40"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"},{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Inspect loom CLI for task design access","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"96c2d78e-0006-4f83-9f1e-c34c7d4033e0","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"which loom; cd /work/ws && loom --help 2>&1 | head -40; cd /work/ws && loom data --help 2>&1 | head -40","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\nloom - Agent Management CLI\n\nManage Claude Code agents working in parallel across workspace repos.\n\nGETTING STARTED\n  1. Select a FleetDB-backed workspace with registered repos.\n\n  2. Create tasks for agents to work on:\n     loom task create --title=\"Add login feature\" --type=feature --priority=2\n\n  3. Run agents:\n     loom plan falcon    # Creates design, sets status=review\n     loom lead           # Review and approve plans\n     loom task falcon    # Implements approved design\n\nKEY CONCEPTS\n  Workspaces   FleetDB-backed repo groups where agents work independently.\n\n  Agents       Claude processes that work on tasks:\n               - 'plan' agent: researches and creates designs\n               - 'task' agent: implements approved designs\n\n  FleetDB      Issue tracker. Tasks flow through states:\n               open → in_progress → review → open → closed\n\n  Auto Mode    --auto flag runs agents continuously, processing multiple\n               tasks until stopped (Ctrl+C) or idle timeout.\n\nCOMMANDS\n  plan         Run a planning agent (creates designs, marks for review)\n  task         Run an implementation agent (implements approved tasks)\n  lead         Interactive mode for reviewing plans and managing backlog\n  monitor      Dashboard showing agent status and task progress\n  recover      Recover agent from error state (clear stale locks, reset tasks)\n  push         Push worktree branches to target with AI conflict resolution\n  pull         Pull integration branch into worktrees with AI conflict resolution\n  sync         Full sync: push all completed work, then pull into all worktrees\n  reset        Hard reset worktrees to a specific branch\n  list         List all agents and their status\n\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\n","stderr":"","executionTime":79,"interleavedOutput":"/installed-agent/loom-marathon/bin/loom\nloom - Agent Management CLI\n\nManage Claude Code agents working in parallel across workspace repos.\n\nGETTING STARTED\n  1. Select a FleetDB-backed workspace with registered repos.\n\n  2. Create tasks for agents to work on:\n     loom task create --title=\"Add login feature\" --type=feature --priority=2\n\n  3. Run agents:\n     loom plan falcon    # Creates design, sets status=review\n     loom lead           # Review and approve plans\n     loom task falcon    # Implements approved design\n\nKEY CONCEPTS\n  Workspaces   FleetDB-backed repo groups where agents work independently.\n\n  Agents       Claude processes that work on tasks:\n               - 'plan' agent: researches and creates designs\n               - 'task' agent: implements approved designs\n\n  FleetDB      Issue tracker. Tasks flow through states:\n               open → in_progress → review → open → closed\n\n  Auto Mode    --auto flag runs agents continuously, processing multiple\n               tasks until stopped (Ctrl+C) or idle timeout.\n\nCOMMANDS\n  plan         Run a planning agent (creates designs, marks for review)\n  task         Run an implementation agent (implements approved tasks)\n  lead         Interactive mode for reviewing plans and managing backlog\n  monitor      Dashboard showing agent status and task progress\n  recover      Recover agent from error state (clear stale locks, reset tasks)\n  push         Push worktree branches to target with AI conflict resolution\n  pull         Pull integration branch into worktrees with AI conflict resolution\n  sync         Full sync: push all completed work, then pull into all worktrees\n  reset        Hard reset worktrees to a specific branch\n  list         List all agents and their status\n\nThe 'loom data' subtree contains thin CLI commands that interact\nwith the configured loom issue backend. When --server or LOOM_SERVER_URL is\nset, commands talk to that loom server over HTTP. Without a server, issue\ncommands use the local backend selected by the workspace configuration and\ndaemon IPC environment.\n\nUse 'loom data' commands when:\n  • You want a backend-aware command surface for agents and scripts.\n  • You want to manage agents on a remote loom server.\n  • You are scripting against a hosted loom deployment.\n\nExamples:\n  loom data show <id> --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data ready --limit 10\n  loom data list --server http://localhost:8080 -o json | jq '.[].id'\n  loom data monitor --server http://localhost:8080\n  loom data agent stop falcon --server http://localhost:8080\n\nRoot-level --server / --workspace are mirrored into LOOM_SERVER_URL /\nLOOM_WORKSPACE in PersistentPreRunE, so 'loom --server URL data show ID'\nand 'loom data show ID --server URL' resolve identically. The data\nsubcommand reads from env, not from its own flag.\n\nUsage:\n  loom data [command]\n\nAvailable Commands:\n  agent       Control a single agent on the loom server (stop/start/restart/yield)\n  agents      List agents managed by the loom server daemon (HTTP)\n  blocked     List issues that are blocked by other open issues (HTTP)\n  claim       Atomically claim an issue\n  close       Close an issue (HTTP)\n  comment     Add a comment to an issue (HTTP)\n  create      Create an issue\n  list        List issues (HTTP)\n  monitor     Show monitor dashboard from a loom server (HTTP, single-shot)\n  ready       List issues that are ready to work on (HTTP)\n  show        Show a single issue by ID (HTTP)\n  update      Update issue fields\n\n","localExecutionTimeMs":38},"isBackground":false},"description":"Inspect loom CLI for task design access"},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-4a6d5c0b-1d08-491b-a8b0-a0959de37b26-23\nfc_4280e92c-49a8-98c7-825d-5337817199c5_0","startedAtMs":"1787438586470","completedAtMs":"1787438586550"},"model_call_id":"3b2e9dd7-11f5-45ff-b1c8-4618e588c81d-6-boy2","session_id":"96c2d78e-0006-4f83-9f1e-c34c7d4033e0","timestamp_ms":1787438586576}
