{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-f5e1217a-b063-4fda-b04d-e13cdb5f1beb-31\nfc_b5e941fa-4cec-91fc-9f9f-70589d1eaed1_0","tool_call":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cd /work/ws && loom data show MARATHON-3 -o json > /tmp/m3.json 2>/tmp/m3.err; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('/tmp/m3.json'))\ndesign=d['design']\n# print sections of interest\nfor start,end in [\n ('## Data Model','## Files to Create'),\n ('## Files to Create','## Sequencing'),\n ('## Acceptance Criteria','## Testing Strategy'),\n]:\n    i=design.find(start); j=design.find(end)\n    print('====', start, '====')\n    print(design[i:j] if i>=0 else 'MISSING')\n    print()\nPY\n","workingDirectory":"","timeout":30000,"toolCallId":"call-f5e1217a-b063-4fda-b04d-e13cdb5f1beb-31\nfc_b5e941fa-4cec-91fc-9f9f-70589d1eaed1_0","simpleCommands":["cd","loom","python3"],"hasInputRedirect":true,"hasOutputRedirect":true,"parsingResult":{"parsingFailed":false,"executableCommands":[{"name":"cd","args":[{"type":"word","value":"/work/ws"}],"fullText":"cd /work/ws"},{"name":"loom","args":[{"type":"word","value":"data"},{"type":"word","value":"show"},{"type":"word","value":"MARATHON-3"},{"type":"word","value":"-o"},{"type":"word","value":"json"}],"fullText":"loom data show MARATHON-3 -o json"},{"name":"python3","args":[],"fullText":"python3"}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":false,"redirects":[{"operator":">","destinationFds":[1],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/m3.json"},{"operator":">","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"word","targetText":"/tmp/m3.err"},{"operator":"<<","destinationFds":[0],"targetNodeType":"heredoc_redirect","targetText":"python3"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Parse design Data Model and AC sections","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"96c2d78e-0006-4f83-9f1e-c34c7d4033e0","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"cd /work/ws && loom data show MARATHON-3 -o json > /tmp/m3.json 2>/tmp/m3.err; python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd=json.load(open('/tmp/m3.json'))\ndesign=d['design']\n# print sections of interest\nfor start,end in [\n ('## Data Model','## Files to Create'),\n ('## Files to Create','## Sequencing'),\n ('## Acceptance Criteria','## Testing Strategy'),\n]:\n    i=design.find(start); j=design.find(end)\n    print('====', start, '====')\n    print(design[i:j] if i>=0 else 'MISSING')\n    print()\nPY\n","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"==== ## Data Model ====\n## Data Model\n\n### Migration version 1\n\nApplied via `schema_migrations` after version 0 bootstrap from MARATHON-2. **Backward compatible** with empty product schema (additive). On existing DBs with only version 0, migrate forward once.\n\n#### Table `users`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | PK, UUID4 string |\n| `username` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UNIQUE |\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Encoded scrypt parameters + salt + hash (single string; document format in module docstring) |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NULL | |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC ISO-8601 with `Z` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\n| `updated_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Same format; set on create |\n\nIndexes: `UNIQUE(username)`.\n\n#### Table `auth_tokens`\n\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `token_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | PK; hex SHA-256 of raw token |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` ON DELETE CASCADE |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | UTC `Z` |\n\nIndex: `user_id` (for future revoke-all).\n\n**No Redis keys** for auth. **No email column.**\n\n### Password hash string format (normative for implementers)\n\nStore one TEXT value, e.g. `scrypt$N=2^14$r=8$p=1$<salt_b64>$<hash_b64>` (exact parameter tuning may vary but must be stable and verified on login). Salt ≥ 16 bytes from `secrets`.\n\n### Token generation\n\n- Raw token: `secrets.token_urlsafe(32)` (always length ≥ 16).\n- Persist only `hashlib.sha256(raw_token.encode(\"ascii\")).hexdigest()`.\n- Compare presented token by hashing then PK lookup (constant-time compare optional once looked up by hash).\n\n### Schema change summary\n\n| Change | Compatible? |\n|--------|-------------|\n| Add `users`, `auth_tokens`; insert migration version 1 | Yes — additive on greenfield / version 0 DBs |\n\n\n\n==== ## Files to Create ====\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/auth/__init__.py` | Package marker; optionally re-export router + `get_current_user`. |\n| `server/auth/passwords.py` | Hash / verify helpers (`scrypt`). |\n| `server/auth/tokens.py` | Mint raw token; hash; insert row; resolve hash → `user_id`. |\n| `server/auth/users.py` | Create user; fetch by id/username; map row → `UserObj` dict. |\n| `server/auth/deps.py` | `get_current_user` FastAPI dependency; 401 envelope helper. |\n| `server/auth/routes.py` | `APIRouter` with register / login / me. |\n| `server/errors.py` | Small helper to build `JSONResponse` error envelopes (shared). |\n| `tests/test_auth.py` | Contract tests: register 201, duplicate 409, validation 400, login 200/401, me 200/401, cross-DB identity (same sqlite path / TestClient). |\n\n### Modify\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.py` | Add `migrate(conn)` / `ensure_schema(sqlite_path)` applying version 1 DDL; keep existing bootstrap. Prefer a list of `(version, sql_callable)` migrations. Expose `connect(sqlite_path) -> Connection` used by auth (WAL pragmas every time). |\n| `server/app.py` | Call full schema ensure on lifespan (not only bootstrap); `include_router` auth routes; leave `/api/health` and stub `GET /` unchanged. |\n| `requirements.txt` | **No new dependencies required** if using stdlib crypto + uuid. Do not add Redis usage for auth. |\n| `tests/test_health.py` | Only if lifespan/migration changes break bootstrap assertions — keep health unauthenticated; do not weaken existing checks. |\n\n### Do not touch\n\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `start.sh` | Supervisor already shares `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`; no auth-specific change |\n| `server/settings.py` | Already exposes sqlite path |\n| `timer.sh`, `loom-prompts/**` | Harness |\n| SPA / `GET /` HTML | MARATHON-16 |\n| Profile PATCH routes | MARATHON-4 |\n\n\n\n==== ## Acceptance Criteria ====\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n1. `POST /api/auth/register` with valid `{username,password}` → **201**, JSON body has `user` (`UserObj` keys exactly as specified, no `email`) and `token` with **len(token) ≥ 16**.\n2. Duplicate username → **409** with error envelope `code=conflict`.\n3. Invalid username or password &lt; 8 → **400** with `code=validation_error`.\n4. `POST /api/auth/login` with correct credentials → **200** and `{user,token}` (new token).\n5. Login with wrong password or unknown user → **401** `unauthorized` (same handling for both; **must not** 404).\n6. `GET /api/auth/me` with `Authorization: Bearer <token>` from register or login → **200** `{user}` matching the registered user.\n7. `/me` without header, with bad token, or with non-Bearer scheme → **401**.\n8. **Cluster:** token minted via `:8000` is accepted by `/api/auth/me` on `:8001` and `:8002` while `./start.sh` is running (shared SQLite).\n9. **Negative:** responses must **not** include `email`; passwords must **not** appear in any response body.\n10. **Negative:** `/api/health` must still return unenveloped `{\"status\":\"ok\",\"node_id\":N}` without auth.\n11. **Negative:** auth data must **not** be stored only in process memory or only in Redis.\n12. Users and tokens survive node process restart (SQLite file under `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR`).\n\n\n\n","stderr"